# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for ci.yml's `sanitizers / tsan` job (.github/sanitizers/run.sh).
#
# An entry hides a report that is not a race in libcvc, or a known race that has its own fix in
# flight. Each entry gets a comment saying which report it hides and why that is safe, or which PR
# fixes it. Format: <type>:<pattern>, one per line, where <type> is race, race_top, thread, mutex,
# signal, deadlock or called_from_lib, and <pattern> matches a function, file or module name in
# the report's stacks (https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions).

# exec_coordinator::start() held its leader_mu_ while it announced its election on the message
# bus, whose dispatch can reach accept_leader(), which takes leader_mu_: a lock-order inversion
# with the bus's lock, reported 6 times in state_exec_coordinator_test and
# state_exec_integration_test. A real bug, fixed in transfix/libcvc#863; remove this entry when
# that lands. Matches only reports with start() itself in a stack, not start_election().
deadlock:cvc::state_exec::exec_coordinator::start()

# pycvc's evaluator.stats(), evaluator_state.stats and process.state didn't keep their owner
# alive (pycvc.i's %pythonappend for them was never generated), so
# test_pycvc_state_exec_eval.py read them after Python freed the owner: 13 heap-use-after-free
# reports, in exactly these five reads (TSan files a use after free under race). A real bug,
# fixed in transfix/libcvc#864; remove these entries when that lands.
race:_wrap_evaluator_state_done_get
race:_wrap_evaluator_state_stack_get
race:_wrap_evaluation_stats_get_step_count
race:_wrap_evaluation_stats_is_complete
race:_wrap_evaluation_stats_elapsed_seconds
